@startuml
title UML - Implemented authenticated finality, suspense and linked returns
autonumber
actor "Provider callback fixture" as Provider
boundary "Axum evidence ingress" as API
control "Payments" as Payments
database "Payments store" as Store
control "Durable worker" as Worker
control "Core financial authority" as Core
database "Core immutable ledger" as Ledger
control "Controls" as Controls
actor "Customer / authorized workforce" as User

Provider -> API : POST signed RailEvidence or CreditEvidence
API -> Payments : verify live HMAC and timestamp; validate typed scope
alt invalid signature or stale packet
 Payments --> API : authentication failure
 API --> Provider : 401
else authenticated financial-scope / identity conflict
 Payments -> Store : immutable quarantine packet + digest + reason
 Payments -> Controls : durable audit and owned investigation case
 API --> Provider : 409
else exact new receipt or duplicate
 Payments -> Store : original evidence identity + full digest; durable acceptance
 note right of Store
 Global evidence ID cannot be reused across types.
 A replay never overwrites original financial facts.
 end note
 API --> Provider : 202 (accepted for processing)
end

group Outgoing finality
 Worker -> Payments : resume original payment
 Payments -> Core : recover finality receipt, otherwise apply archived packet
 Core -> Core : HMAC integrity + exact original scope
 alt SETTLED and no prior financial receipt
  Core -> Ledger : atomic hold consumption + balanced principal/fee journal
  Core -> Ledger : daily usage POSTED + immutable finality receipt
 else REJECTED or CANCELLED
  Core -> Ledger : exact submitted hold release + usage RELEASED + finality
 else prior receipt
  Ledger --> Core : same immutable result / batch
 end
 Core --> Payments : authoritative financial outcome
 note over Payments,Core
 Lost acknowledgment is recovered by original business identity.
 Pending/NOT_FOUND never releases funds.
 Contradictory final evidence cannot release a consumed hold.
 end note
 Payments -> Store : settle / decline / cancel only against Core receipt
end

group Incoming or original-linked return
 Worker -> Payments : resume original credit movement
 Payments -> Core : verify archived packet; record movement
 Core -> Core : derive target and owner from Core reference / original payer
 alt RETURN_SETTLED
  Core -> Ledger : lock original settled payment; sum all accepted returns
  Ledger --> Core : accepted total + new principal <= original principal
  note right of Core
  Includes unallocated suspense principal.
  Original journal, fee and gross daily usage remain intact.
  end note
 end
 Core -> Ledger : one balanced clearing -> suspense journal + movement receipt
 Core --> Payments : target / original customer / suspense receipt
 alt unknown, closed or credit-restricted target
  Payments -> Controls : owned payment case; retain funds in suspense
 else known eligible destination
  Payments -> Controls : signed current checks for Core-derived customer
  alt pending, review or deny
   Controls --> Payments : current outcome
   Payments -> Controls : retain suspense; own review / denied handling
  else current allow
   Controls --> Payments : bound signed decisions
   Payments -> Core : allocate exact movement with trusted expiring permit
   Core -> Core : ordered account locks; recheck current destination and permit
   Core -> Ledger : atomic suspense -> customer journal + allocation receipt
   Core --> Payments : same allocation receipt on retry
   Payments -> Store : CREDITED + versioned fact / durable audit
  end
 end
end

User -> API : scoped payment / credit / quarantine inquiry
API -> Core : authoritative booking, allocation and return totals
API --> User : original SETTLED payment + separate return summary / history
note over API,User
Only Core allocation makes incoming funds available.
Unconfirmed DRAFT cancellation has no financial effect.
Submitted cancellation uses the separate original-identity recovery workflow.
end note
@enduml
